== 6.9 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The commonest fish farmed in Nigeria is the],
  [carp],
  [African catfish],
  [Nile tilapia],
  [mullet]
)

#mcq(2, [The scientific name of the African catfish is],
  [Clarias gariepinus],
  [Oreochromis niloticus],
  [Cyprinus carpio],
  [Mugil cephalus]
)

#mcq(3, [Tilapia is less favoured than catfish in ponds because it],
  [cannot eat plankton],
  [grows too slowly everywhere],
  [needs salt water],
  [breeds too freely and overpopulates the pond]
)

#mcq(4, [A pond should be sited on soil that is],
  [clayey and holds water],
  [sandy and drains],
  [stony and steep],
  [peaty and acid]
)

#mcq(5, [The recommended depth of an earthen fish pond is],
  [5 m],
  [0.2 m],
  [1.0–1.5 m],
  [10 m]
)

#mcq(6, [Liming a pond before filling is done to],
  [feed the fish],
  [deepen the pond],
  [cool the water],
  [raise the pH and kill pests]
)

#mcq(7, [Pond fertilisation with poultry manure is done to],
  [raise the pH],
  [clear the water],
  [kill the fish],
  [grow the plankton the fish eat]
)

#mcq(8, [A pond is stocked with fingerlings at],
  [100 per m²],
  [5–10 fingerlings per m²],
  [1 000 per m²],
  [1 per 100 m²]
)

#mcq(9, [Fingerlings should be acclimatised before release because],
  [they must be fed first],
  [they need to be counted],
  [a sudden temperature change kills them],
  [the pond is salty]
)

#mcq(10, [Pond fish are fed each day at about],
  [3 per cent of body weight],
  [30 per cent of body weight],
  [0.03 per cent],
  [100 per cent]
)

#mcq(11, [Fish coming to the surface and gasping indicates],
  [low oxygen in the water],
  [the presence of tilapia],
  [a rise in temperature only],
  [too much feed]
)

#mcq(12, [Green pond water is a sign that],
  [plankton are growing well],
  [the lime was excessive],
  [the pond is polluted],
  [the fish are diseased]
)

#mcq(13, [A scum on the pond surface usually means],
  [the water is too cold],
  [the fish are breeding],
  [too much feed is being given],
  [the lime is too fresh]
)

#mcq(14, [Harvesting a pond by draining is called],
  [complete harvesting],
  [partial harvesting],
  [seining],
  [trapping]
)

#mcq(15, [Smoking is used to preserve fish because it],
  [dries the flesh and deposits preservative smoke],
  [adds protein],
  [kills all bacteria],
  [increases the weight]
)

#mcq(16, [Integrated fish farming is the],
  [combination of a pond with poultry or a piggery],
  [farming of fish and rice],
  [use of a cage in a river],
  [growing of two fish species]
)

#mcq(17, [Rice–fish culture is risky because],
  [the water is too deep],
  [the rice needs no water],
  [the fish eat the rice],
  [pesticides used on the rice may kill the fish]
)

#mcq(18, [Cage culture is attractive because the farmer],
  [needs no market],
  [needs no fingerlings],
  [needs no feed],
  [needs no land, only a cage in the water]
)

#mcq(19, [A fish pond should have its inlet and outlet],
  [both at the bottom],
  [at opposite ends],
  [side by side],
  [both above the water]
)

#mcq(20, [Predators of pond fish include],
  [tilapia],
  [plankton],
  [birds, snakes and otters],
  [water lettuce]
)

#mcq(21, [Forestry is important in Nigeria because forests],
  [prevent all erosion],
  [increase the rainfall everywhere],
  [replace farmland],
  [protect watersheds and supply timber and fuel]
)

#mcq(22, [Land set aside by government to protect timber, water and wildlife is],
  [a plantation cleared every year],
  [protected government land for timber, water and wildlife],
  [a fish pond],
  [a private farm]
)

#mcq(23, [A plantation is best described as],
  [a natural forest left alone],
  [trees planted and managed as a crop],
  [a shelterbelt],
  [a sacred grove]
)

#mcq(24, [Taungya is a system in which],
  [bees are kept in a forest],
  [cattle graze under trees],
  [crops are grown between young forest trees],
  [fish are grown with rice]
)

#mcq(25, [Alley cropping is the growing of],
  [trees on a boundary only],
  [two crops in one row],
  [crops between hedgerows of trees],
  [trees between rows of fish ponds]
)

#mcq(26, [Trees planted across the prevailing wind are meant to],
  [shade the fish pond],
  [increase the rainfall],
  [mark the boundary],
  [reduce wind speed and protect the crop]
)

#mcq(27, [A shelterbelt is],
  [several rows of trees protecting a farm or a village],
  [a fence of wire],
  [a hedge of grass],
  [a single tree]
)

#mcq(28, [A woodlot is kept for],
  [honey only],
  [fuel, poles and small timber],
  [fish],
  [grazing]
)

#mcq(29, [Cutting only the mature trees in a forest is called],
  [cutting the smallest trees],
  [cutting only the mature trees and leaving the young ones],
  [burning the undergrowth],
  [clearing the whole forest]
)

#mcq(30, [The mangrove forest is important because it],
  [grows on dry hills],
  [supplies wool],
  [produces wheat],
  [protects the coast and shelters fish nurseries]
)

#mcq(31, [Gmelina and teak are grown mainly for],
  [poles and timber],
  [fruit],
  [honey],
  [latex]
)

#mcq(32, [Shea butter comes from the],
  [rubber tree],
  [shea tree],
  [cocoa tree],
  [oil palm]
)

#mcq(33, [Tannin from tree bark is used in],
  [bread baking],
  [soap making],
  [leather tanning],
  [fish smoking]
)

#mcq(34, [A sacred grove is best described as],
  [a cleared farm],
  [a patch of forest protected by custom],
  [a government plantation],
  [a riverside garden]
)

#mcq(35, [Agroforestry is the practice of],
  [planting only trees],
  [clearing all trees before planting],
  [rearing fish under trees],
  [growing trees with crops or livestock on the same land]
)

#mcq(36, [A farmer with a 100 m² pond stocking 8 fingerlings per m² needs],
  [8 000 fingerlings],
  [80 fingerlings],
  [800 fingerlings],
  [108 fingerlings]
)

#mcq(37, [A pond of 250 m² stocked at 6 fish per m² holds],
  [1 500 fish],
  [2 500 fish],
  [600 fish],
  [150 fish]
)

#mcq(38, [The main reason fish farming is popular in the south is that],
  [the south has no rivers],
  [swamps and floodplains are unsuitable for crops but good for ponds],
  [fish need no feeding],
  [the north has no market]
)

#mcq(39, [Forest fires are dangerous because they],
  [kill only the grass],
  [help the trees to grow],
  [improve the soil],
  [destroy seedlings and the humus layer]
)

#mcq(40, [Overgrazing a forest reserve damages it because],
  [the animals add manure only],
  [the trees grow faster],
  [the animals plant seeds],
  [the stock eats the seedlings and compacts the soil]
)

